🦖 Example <p>Lets route an invoice based on its status code.  </p> <pre><code># Lets decide what happens to this invoice
status = 'overdue'

if status == 'paid':
    print('File it.')
elif status == 'pending':
    print('Wait.')
elif status == 'overdue':
    print('Send a reminder.')
else:
    print('Unknown status, flag for review.')
</code></pre> <p>Output: <code>Send a reminder.</code> </p> Why not just use a bunch of separate if statements? <p>Because elif stops as soon as one matches. Separate if statements all get checked, and more than one can fire. That difference will bite you eventually, so we cover it properly in detecting multiple features.  </p>
